1
00:00:00,330 --> 00:00:02,630
Tap your phone with a pen. Nothing.

2
00:00:02,660 --> 00:00:05,320
Tap it with a finger, and it works. Why?

3
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:09,090
Under the glass sits an invisible grid of wires,

4
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:11,700
holding a tiny electric charge.

5
00:00:11,730 --> 00:00:14,080
Your body is mostly salty water,

6
00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:15,800
so your finger conducts.

7
00:00:15,830 --> 00:00:18,690
Touch the glass, and it pulls a little charge away,

8
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:20,100
right at that spot.

9
00:00:20,130 --> 00:00:21,810
The phone feels that dip,

10
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:23,830
and knows exactly where you are.

11
00:00:24,430 --> 00:00:28,200
A plastic pen is an insulator. It takes no charge,

12
00:00:28,230 --> 00:00:30,500
so the screen never notices it.

13
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:33,700
Give the pen a conductive tip, and suddenly,

14
00:00:33,730 --> 00:00:35,300
it's a finger too.
